# Container image CVE exceptions.
# GENERATED by scripts/gen_trivyignore.py from security/accepted-risks.yml --
# do not hand-edit. Edit the registry and regenerate.
# Security acceptance standard (operator, 2026-10-08; shared with
# datawatch-app, dmz006/datawatch#197). See security/accepted-risks.yml's
# header for the schema, and scripts/check_accepted_risks.py for the lint.

# zlib1g -- CVE-2023-45853
# severity: critical; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# Integer overflow in inflate(). Only exploitable processing attacker-controlled
# deflate streams with a specific window size. curl and git in this image
# decompress only trusted responses from operator-configured remotes; not
# network-exposed via datawatch APIs.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
CVE-2023-45853

# libsqlite3-0 -- CVE-2025-7458, CVE-2026-11822, CVE-2026-11824
# severity: critical/high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# SQLite used internally by the gh CLI binary; not exposed via datawatch
# REST/MCP APIs. CVE-2025-7458: integer overflow. CVE-2026-11822/11824: FTS5
# full-text-search memory corruption via crafted database pages -- exploitable
# only against attacker-controlled SQLite databases; gh CLI processes only
# trusted local cached GitHub state, not attacker-supplied databases.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
CVE-2025-7458
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# curl, libcurl4 -- CVE-2026-6276
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# Cookie leak on cross-origin redirect. curl is used by agent tooling for REST
# API calls to operator-configured endpoints.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
CVE-2026-6276

# libldap-2.5-0 -- CVE-2023-2953
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# Null pointer dereference in ber_memalloc_x via malformed LDAP response.
# OpenLDAP not directly used; pulled transitively by OpenSSH. No LDAP
# connections made from within the container.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
