CVE-2025-69720

# perl, perl-base, perl-modules-5.36, libperl5.36 -- CVE-2026-9538
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# Archive::Tar memory corruption via crafted tar archive. Perl is a transitive
# dependency of git/gnupg; the datawatch service does not execute Perl scripts
# or call Archive::Tar, and does not extract tar archives at runtime.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm. GH#163 (2026-10-07) already removed
# CVE-2026-42496/42497/48962/8376 from this block once a fix shipped for those
# four -- same removal process applies here if/when one ships.
CVE-2026-9538

# git-lfs -- CVE-2025-26625
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# git-lfs may write to arbitrary files via crafted LFS pointer refs from a
# malicious LFS server. Only exploitable when cloning/pulling from an
# attacker-controlled git remote. All git remotes in this image are
# operator-configured; no untrusted LFS servers are contacted.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
CVE-2025-26625

# python3.11, libpython3.11-* -- CVE-2026-7210, CVE-2025-69534
# severity: critical/high; images: agent-aider, agent-gemini
# Python 3.11 installed in agent images for aider and other Python-based tools;
# the datawatch service itself is Go. CVE-2026-7210:
# xml.parsers.expat/ElementTree use-after-free via crafted XML -- agent tooling
# does not expose Python XML parsers to untrusted input. CVE-2025-69534:
# python-markdown DoS via malformed HTML-like input -- no untrusted content
# piped through python-markdown by the core service.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
CVE-2026-7210
CVE-2025-69534

