# sudo -- CVE-2026-96512
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# TZ-based bypass of sudoers NOTBEFORE/NOTAFTER time restrictions. The
# containers configure no time-restricted sudoers rules and run a single trusted
# agent user. Present in every agent image via the base.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
CVE-2026-96512

# libssl3 -- CVE-2026-84782
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full, stats-cluster
# DTLS retransmission logic flaw in OpenSSL. DTLS is TLS over UDP (WebRTC, CoAP,
# some VPNs); datawatch's containers serve and call only regular TCP-based
# TLS/HTTPS, never originating or accepting a DTLS connection -- the flawed code
# path is never reached. Phase 1's live rescan found this spans all 5 images,
# not only stats-cluster as originally scoped when it blocked v8.35.0's release
# CI.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
CVE-2026-84782

# python3.11, libpython3.11-* -- CVE-2026-19553
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-gemini
# Certificate verification bypass via missing server_hostname validation in
# ssl.SSLContext.wrap_bio(). Whether agent-gemini's Python runtime actually
# calls wrap_bio() (vs. the higher-level wrap_socket()/create_default_context()
# paths most HTTP clients use, which are unaffected) was not independently
# traced before suppressing -- only that no Debian fix exists.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm. NOT independently traced (self-admitted
# caveat) -- re-review should actually trace which TLS call path agent-gemini's
# code uses, the way CVE-2026-19445 was traced this session.
CVE-2026-19553

# http-cache-semantics (npm) -- CVE-2026-93748
# severity: high; images: agent-gemini
# Information disclosure via the max-stale cache-control directive. Transitive
# dependency of @google/gemini-cli's own package.json. Whether any gemini-cli
# dependency path actually exercises max-stale-aware caching against
# attacker-influenced content (vs. just Google's own API responses) was not
# independently traced.
# No newer published npm version exists as of this migration. NOT independently
# traced (self-admitted caveat). Unlike most entries here this is an actively
# maintained package, not a slow Debian backport -- check for a fix each cycle,
# not just on expiry.
CVE-2026-93748

# libpython3.11-minimal -- CVE-2026-19445
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-gemini
# Use-after-free of a server-side SSLContext when sni_callback switches contexts
# mid-handshake (3.11.2-6+deb12u9). Grepped every installed Python package
# (stdlib + both images' full site-packages, including agent-aider's pipx venv)
# for sni_callback: zero hits anywhere except the stdlib's own ssl.py attribute
# definition. aiohttp.worker does build a server-side SSLContext, but the only
# aiohttp importers found in agent-aider are Google auth's async client
# transport wrappers, not a server. The vulnerable code path is confirmed
# unreachable.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm. Independently traced and confirmed
# unreachable this session -- re-check for a fix each cycle; re-trace only if
# either tool's dependency tree changes meaningfully.
# TRACED: grep of installed site-packages in networkless container (docker run
# --entrypoint /bin/sh --network none)
CVE-2026-19445

# libexpat1 -- CVE-2026-77214
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# Heap buffer over-read in XML_ParseBuffer, triggered by
# malformed/attacker-controlled XML. Scanned every file in the image for a
# dynamic link to libexpat1: only /usr/lib/git-core/git-http-push links it. That
# binary is git's legacy dumb-HTTP/WebDAV push path, superseded by the
# smart-HTTP protocol git push has used by default since ~2010; it is never
# invoked by any datawatch code path, the image's own git usage, or a normal
# `git push` to a modern remote (GitHub/GitLab/etc. all serve smart HTTP). Even
# in the dumb-HTTP case the exposure is on push, not fetch, requiring the
# operator's own configured remote to be malicious -- not an attacker-controlled
# input.
# Found live by image-refresh.yaml's blocking scan (new since the BL398
# migration baseline -- not in the original 70). No fix available in Debian
# bookworm. Independently traced and confirmed unreachable this session.
# TRACED: ldd scan of every executable in a networkless container (docker run
# --entrypoint /bin/sh --network none) to find every real linker to libexpat1,
# then traced each caller's actual invocation path
CVE-2026-77214

# libgnutls30 -- CVE-2026-88647, CVE-2026-88648
# severity: high; images: agent-base and everything built from it (agent-claude,
# agent-opencode, agent-aider, agent-gemini, agent-goose, parent-full)
# Information disclosure via hostname verification bypass / cross-domain
# certificate restriction bypass via incomplete X.509 validation, in Debian's
# libgnutls30 3.7.9-2+deb12u7. No fixed version listed by Debian for bookworm
# as of 2026-10-09. Found by v9.0.3's release scan (new since v9.0.1/v9.0.2's
# scans -- not a drift of our own pinning, a new upstream disclosure).
# Re-check for a Debian backport each cycle.
CVE-2026-88647
CVE-2026-88648

# gh (GitHub CLI, installed via `install_packages gh`) -- CVE-2026-78667,
# CVE-2026-78669, CVE-2026-97031
# severity: high; images: agent-base and everything built from it (agent-claude,
# agent-opencode, agent-aider, agent-gemini, agent-goose, parent-full)
# These are Go stdlib (net/http, crypto/tls) and golang.org/x/net DoS CVEs
# (HTTP/2 SETTINGS flood, crafted Range headers, ECH outer-extension abuse)
# baked into the gh v2.102.0 binary itself -- gh is pulled as a prebuilt apt
# package, not compiled from source here, so our own Dockerfile.agent-base
# GO_VERSION pin (see check-dockerfile-go-versions.sh) has no effect on it.
# Confirmed v2.102.0 (released 2026-09-30) is cli/cli's latest release as of
# 2026-10-09 -- upstream hasn't cut a build against patched Go/x-net yet.
# Re-check each cycle for a newer gh release.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031
